<title>UK: Lavendon shares set first-day premium.</title>
<headline>Lavendon shares set first-day premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Lavendon Group Plc, a power access equipment fleet operator, set a five percent premium on their first day of trading on the London Stock Exchange on Thursday.</p>
<p>The shares traded at 147-1/2p by 1333 GMT, up 7-1/2p on the price at which they had been placed by broker Beeson Gregory.</p>
<p>The placing gave the company a market capitalisation of 29.8 million stg and raised 11.3 million stg.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
</text>
